{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF TO EPIC 061c (owns the two sidecar files) — RCA CONFIRMED, EXACT FIX DOCUMENTED, NOT YET IMPLEMENTED.\n\nWHY THIS IS BEING REPARENTED, NOT LANDED BY THIS SESSION: the fix must edit src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py and src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py, both on epic 061c's protected file list. 061c has a large in-flight Gerrit stack; editing these from a separate change would collide. Reparenting under 061c so that session lands it within its own stack without disruption. The third site (code_review/sidecar.py) is NOT 061c's but is kept together here so the fix stays one coherent unit (identical mechanism at all three sites).\n\nSTATUS ON CURRENT main (tip 253224f354): the dead session 2b0c5f01 documented a fix in an earlier comment but it NEVER landed — verified all three emit() paths still auto-call prune() on origin/main. So this is still a live defect.\n\nROOT CAUSE (confirmed empirically by the prior session's two-clone harness; mechanism re-verified against current main): each sidecar emit() appends a new UUID-named event and then automatically calls prune(), which uses _store.event_append.delete_events to physically delete older committed UUID event files. Across two independent tracker clones that share the tickets branch, delete(oldest)+add(new-uuid) in each clone makes git's rename detection resolve the shared base file as 'renamed to' a DIFFERENT new UUID in each clone -> rename/rename CONFLICT on union merge, wedging reconvergence. This violates docs/concurrency.md I1 (append-only): 'convergence ... never by deleting a committed event (I1 append-only)' (docs/concurrency.md:168). Prior art: bug 8185-2d4b-d2bf-4282 / commit be8a0c059 removed the identical mechanism from enrich_drain + overlap/digest_sidecar and explicitly spawned THIS ticket for the three siblings. NUANCE: git rename detection is content-similarity based and rebar events are single-line minified JSON, so a one-byte length difference between the pruned and new event can drop similarity below git's 50% threshold and the merge spuriously succeeds — build the two-clone base from a REAL emitted payload (equal-length neighbour) or the repro looks green. This is why the wedge is intermittent in production and then permanent.\n\nEXACT FIX (net -3 executable lines in src/, prune() kept as operator-invoked):\n  1. src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py — DELETE line 89: 'prune(verdict.get(\"ticket_id\", \"\"), repo_root=repo_root)  # best-effort retention'. Keep line 90 'return True'.\n  2. src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py — DELETE line 148: 'prune(target_ticket, repo_root=repo_root)  # best-effort retention (bounds code-review growth)'. Keep line 149 'return True'.\n  3. src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py — DELETE line 59: 'prune(str(verdict.get(\"ticket_id\") or \"\"), repo_root=repo_root)  # best-effort retention'. Keep line 60 'return True'.\n  In all three, prune() itself (the def and its delete_events call) is UNCHANGED and remains importable as an EXPLICIT operator-invoked op — only the AUTOMATIC call from emit() is removed. The prune() return value is unused at the call site, so removal is clean.\n\nTEST CHANGES:\n  - tests/unit/test_audit_retention_cap.py: two tests currently assert the DEFECT and must be INVERTED in place (not deleted), following fix-out -> revise -> verify RED -> fix-in: test_code_review_emit_calls_prune (line 95; 'emit must prune the target ticket after appending', line 101) and test_code_review_emit_retains_the_cap (line 80; asserts emit->prune caps at 50). Re-point them to pin the append-only invariant (emit() appends and does NOT delete any committed event) where the defect used to be. These tests were added by story fde0, which introduced the automatic code-review prune this bug removes; direct-call prune() tests stay untouched and green.\n  - Add real two-clone RED reproductions (bare remote + clones A/B sharing one tickets branch, base padded to the retention bound from a real emitted payload, both clones offline, one automatic emit each) for each of the three emit paths: pre-fix -> rename/rename CONFLICT; post-fix -> clean union reconverge (rc=0). Run under the full concurrency tier + mutation check (re-add the prune() call -> back to RED).\n\nFILE IMPACT: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py, src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py, src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py, tests/unit/test_audit_retention_cap.py, plus new two-clone repro test(s). ACs unchanged (see description).\n\nDEFERRED TRADEOFF: removing automatic prune means sidecar event files grow unbounded per ticket. Merge-safe bounded retention is deliberately deferred and tracked separately as 475e-9b99-9085-4b2d. SIBLING SWEEP was clean: after this fix, every remaining delete_events call sits inside an explicit operator-invoked prune() (e.g. purge_bridge.py behind 'rebar purge-bridge') — zero automatic invocations remain in src/rebar.\n\nDEFECT LEGITIMACY: defect (violates cited I1 append-only invariant + prior closed bug 8185 for the identical mechanism). Caller/dependency gate: prune() retained for operators; only the automatic emit-time call is removed, so no caller depending on emit's return (a bool) is affected."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785616523885133001,"uuid":"3f0aeaf9-6dba-4fda-9433-418e1d62b0b7"}